{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":57747,"duration_api_ms":57265,"num_turns":10,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"2d29607e-9383-413b-ac40-f0bc8e5e93ac","total_cost_usd":0.3547035,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":30878,"cache_read_input_tokens":241552,"output_tokens":1636,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":30878,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":8,"outputTokens":1636,"cacheReadInputTokens":241552,"cacheCreationInputTokens":30878,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.3547035,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"All three amendments identify real, verified issues. The failing test is confirmed (TAN=2.168, adults drop to 2, 0 juveniles). The migration signature prevents error propagation from malformed saves. The pre-step invariant enforcement mutates state (e.g. clamping ph, truncating event_log) before reaching hard failures, leaving engine in a modified state on error.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-3-5d8c9ede","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: `cargo test -p tank_core hatch_produces_juveniles` fails with adults=2, juveniles=0, TAN=2.168 mg/L. This is a concrete test failure on the current branch that blocks CI. Whether the fix is retuning the test fixture or correcting nitrogen cycle dynamics, it must be addressed."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-6289fe3d","decision":"accept","rationale":"Confirmed in save.rs:29 that `MigrationFn = fn(&mut Value)` is infallible. `migrate_v2_to_v3` silently returns on missing `state` or `water` (lines 207-209, 241-243) rather than reporting the error. With only two migrations (one is a no-op), converting to `fn(&mut Value) -> Result<(), SimError>` is a minimal change now that avoids a larger refactor later when more complex migrations (field renames, type transforms) arrive. This is a legitimate robustness improvement."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-e6606032","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified in invariants.rs and engine.rs:490-491. `step_hours` calls `enforce_invariants(&mut self.state)?` as a pre-step check. This function mutates state extensively before reaching hard failure checks: it clamps ph (line 95), clamps lid_exchange_factor/light/filter/aeration/indices (lines 109-136), truncates event_log (lines 212-214), and more — all before reaching `check_unit_interval` and `check_sum_close_to_one` (lines 185-210) which can return errors. A state with `ph=9.0` gets clamped to 8.5 even if a later check like `shrimp_assimilation_efficiency=1.2` fails. This is a real correctness bug: callers expect that a failed step leaves the engine unchanged."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"bc9c8879-13c1-41c2-8b5d-39427006aa57"}
